infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same predicate, two placements
  desc o.status = 'shipped' on the outer table — in ON it filters the match; in WHERE it silently demotes LEFT to INNER
  compares
    - label Condition in ON
      children
        - label Decides which orders count as a match
          desc Runs before NULL-extension, against the product
        - label Unmatched users stay, NULL-extended
          desc A user with no shipped order still appears once
        - label LEFT keeps its outer semantics
          desc ON o.user_id = u.id AND o.status = 'shipped'
        - label Home for any predicate on the right table
          desc The match condition belongs here, not in WHERE
    - label Condition in WHERE
      children
        - label Filters the final result rows
          desc Runs after NULL-extension, on the joined output
        - label NULL = 'shipped' is UNKNOWN, row dropped
          desc WHERE treats UNKNOWN as false and discards it
        - label Every unmatched user is erased
          desc LEFT JOIN now behaves exactly like INNER JOIN
        - label Only safe use: WHERE o.id IS NULL
          desc Deliberately keeps only unmatched rows — the anti-join
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
